1071
00:51:08,020 --> 00:51:10,550
And so it's like we took
our previous value function.

1072
00:51:10,550 --> 00:51:13,810
We do our Bellman backup, and
we get a new value function.

1073
00:51:13,810 --> 00:51:16,480
And we do this over and over
and over again until our value

1074
00:51:16,480 --> 00:51:18,890
function stops changing.

1075
00:51:18,890 --> 00:51:22,100
So for policy iteration, we kept
going until our policy stops

1076
00:51:22,100 --> 00:51:22,830
changing.

1077
00:51:22,830 --> 00:51:26,420
Here we keep going until our
value function stops changing.

1078
00:51:26,420 --> 00:51:29,610
And what that condition
means is it says,

1079
00:51:29,610 --> 00:51:31,250
I keep going until
the difference

1080
00:51:31,250 --> 00:51:34,040
between my old value of estate
and my new value of estate

1081
00:51:34,040 --> 00:51:36,590
is really small
for all the states.

1082
